W: 1. Betsy Bell and Mary Gray
W: They were bonny lasses
W: They bigget a bower on yon burnside
W: And theekit it o'er wi rashes.
W:
W: 2. They theekit it o'er wi rashes green
W: They theekit it o'er wi heather
W: But the plague came from the burrow town
W: And slew them baith thegither.
W:
W: 3. They would not wear their shoes of red
W: Nor would they wear them yellow
W: But they would wear their shoes of green
W: To ride through the streets of Yarrow.
W:
W: 4. They thought to lie in Methren Kirk yard
W: Among their noble kin
W: But they must lie in Stronach haugh
W: All out beneath the sun.
W:
W: 5. Betsy Bell and Mary Gray
W: They were bonny lasses
W: They bigget a bower on yon burnside
W: And theekit it o'er wi rashes.
